{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>An everlasting statute, etc.</b> From here is a hammer to strike the head of the one who errs in saying that fat was forbidden only that of consecrated offerings — for behold it is written ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם בְּכָל מוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶם״, and how could this verse stand if nothing was forbidden except the fat of consecrated offerings? Thus did Torat Kohanim expound: ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם״ — for the House of the World to Come; ״לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם״ — that it shall apply for the generations; ״בְּכֹל מוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶם״ — in the Land and outside the Land — end quote. Now, after it said ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם״, what place is there to say <b>for your generations, in all your dwellings</b>? Rather, it is certain that the intention is along this line: ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם״ continues from what is above, which concerns the matter of consecrated offerings, and He said that there shall be an additional warning for your generations in all your dwellings: ״כָּל חֵלֶב״ etc. — meaning that the prohibition of fat shall apply for your generations in all your dwellings, even outside the Land. For you might have thought that He forbade it only at a time when there is offering upon the altar and not at other times; or even at a time when it is not being offered, if it is in a place where it is offered — but in a place where it is not offered, not so — Scripture comes to teach: ״לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם בְּכֹל מוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶם״. And if the one who errs should claim that only the fat of an animal fit for offering is forbidden — after it already said ״חֻקַּת עוֹלָם״, what room is there for such error that necessitated saying ״לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם בְּכֹל מוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶם״?"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:52:55.125200595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}